sparky-stereo-audio 0.3.1 (2026-11-19)
  * ORDER 757: a graphics card's HDMI or DisplayPort sound is no longer "could not be read" when no sound is playing.
    The reader took an HDA output only when the kernel printed a Device line for it, and for an HDMI codec the kernel
    prints that line only while a PCM is open. The card is now recognised by its codec's HDMI or DP pins and its ELD
    files; its outputs are the displays connected, with the ELD's rates within the converters' rates.
  * No display connected is not a fault. What was read from a display is kept for that display and used while it is away.
  * A display connected or disconnected is noticed by a udev rule on the graphics driver's hotplug event, and the
    service reads the card again until two readings agree.

sparky-stereo-audio 0.3.0 (2026-11-19)
  * General MIDI through a dedicated user service and Debian libfluidsynth, with its audio
    renderer started for notes and released after voices and effects finish.
  * Debian's light soundfont and alternatives, per-person font and MIDI choices,
    a MIDI file handler and translated problems. No image or role list changes.

0.2.0 (2026-11-18)
  * Insert an open binaural filter for multichannel headphone playback while
    keeping stereo direct. Layout and profile choices belong to the engine.
  * Add explicit passive matrix decoding and PSD upmix for multichannel outputs.
    Both are off by default; no matrix-content flag is inferred from stereo.
  * Keep encoded playback on its selected output so the player can retry PCM
    when that output cannot take the encoded format. Expose saved codec choices.
  * Keep policy failures in the existing problems engine, in ten languages.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.0 (2026-11-16)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * ORDER 631 (Daniel, 2026-11-16: "hi fidelity audio is a must across all audio systems ... it's just default configs"): the sound system follows the rate of what plays
  * Rates from the computer's own devices (HDA codecs, displays' audio blocks, USB DACs), 44100 and 48000 Hz always
  * Conversion quality 14 where the processor carries it, measured, else the highest it carries (never below PipeWire's 4)
  * Triangular dither for devices that take only 16 bit; drop-ins named 00-sparky-stereo-audio.conf, so every file of the person wins
  * Failures are said and kept by sparky-stereo-problems, in ten languages
